                <pb facs="0272" n="200" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg200"/>

                <head>No. 109.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. Lowell</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-03-03"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 3,
                        1882</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>[States that the cases of our citizens under arrest in Ireland is the occasion of
                    inquiry in the House of Representatives, and instructs Mr. Lowell to use all
                    diligence in regard to the late cases, especially of Hart and McSweeny, and to
                    report his action by cable.]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
